  "tutorial": {
    ":db/id": 17592186746938,
    ":tutorial/content": "**MTH 341 \u2014 Mini Exam 2 Review**\n\nDue: unknown\nDeadline note: This is an exam review guide. Neither supplied PDF states a submission deadline or the current exam date; no deadline has been inferred from the historical PDF metadata.\nDate imported: 2026-10-29\nQuestion PDF: [MTH341-Mini-Exam2_Review-1.pdf](/api/source?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F341%2FSG-2%2FMTH341-Mini-Exam2_Review-1.pdf)\nSupplied answer key: [ME2 review solutions-1.pdf](/api/source?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F341%2FSG-2%2FME2%20review%20solutions-1.pdf)\nTextbook: [A First Course in Linear Algebra \u2014 Version 2017, Revision A](/api/source?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F341%2FKuttler-LinearAlgebra-AFirstCourse-2017A.pdf), Lyryx Learning, based on K. Kuttler.\n\nStudy answers and worked explanations are authored additions, checked independently and compared with the supplied handwritten key. Alternative valid elementary-matrix factorizations and nonzero scalar multiples of a dependence relation are acceptable.\n\n## Instructions\n\nMini Exam 2 covers textbook \u00a7\u00a72.1.9 (Elementary Matrices), 2.1.10 (More on Matrix Inverses), 3.1 (Basic Techniques and Properties of determinants), 4.10.1 (Spanning Set of Vectors), and 4.10.2 (Linearly Independent Set of Vectors). The review is not exhaustive. If a problem gives you trouble, work more similar problems from the textbook until you are comfortable with the ideas.\n\nThere are five numbered review items: one study direction and four mathematical exercises. Preserve both determinant methods in Problem 3. In Problem 2(c), infer the reversed product from row operations without multiplying the matrices.",
    ":tutorial/id": "8fe816ac-6683-590c-a7f6-eaf00890030f",
    ":tutorial/title": "Assignment information"
  },
